<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco up, Hoare Govett positive.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco up, Hoare Govett positive.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperical Tobacco Plc rose on Wednesday as analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett repeated a postive view on the stock, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 6-1/2p at 387 by 1108 GMT in active trade of 1.4 million shares, continuing a steady rebound since dropping to a low of 351p early last month following the October spin-off from conglomerate Hanson Plc.</p>
<p>Analysts at Hoare Govett were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
